```cpp
void print(const int ia[10])
{
	for (size_t i = 0; i != 10; ++i)
	cout << ia[i] << endl;
}
```

The function prints the all 10 elements of ia. The parameter is wrong, because if we passed a smaller array to print, the for loop will overstep the array's bounds. Since this version of print seems to be intended to print arrays of ints that are exactly of size 10, ia should be a reference to an array of 10 const int. This will limit the acceptable arguments to the desired type of arrays.

correction:

```cpp
void print(const int (&ia)[10])
{
	for (size_t i = 0; i != 10; ++i)
	cout << ia[i] << endl;
}
```

