```

Both a and b should be put in a header. In the case of a, eq is an inline function that is expanded at compile time. "Unlike other functions, inline...functions may be defined multiple times in the program" (p. 240) All of the definition of an inline function must match exactly. The compiler would need the definition in order able to expand the function; not just the declaration. In the case of b, putValues is a declaration of a normal function, which should be put into a header so the compiler could see. Thereafter, it is the job of the linker, not the compiler, to link the declaration with the definition.

